WEBVTT

00:00:01.360 --> 00:00:03.790
It's good to have a job!

00:00:03.790 --> 00:00:05.430
What I wanna be when I grow up?

00:00:05.430 --> 00:00:06.270
Yeah.

00:00:06.270 --> 00:00:09.060
I'd like that to be today's discussion.

00:00:09.330 --> 00:00:12.550
Like usual, that's got nothing to
do with the student council.

00:00:12.550 --> 00:00:17.070
It's rare for us to
actually do our jobs.

00:00:17.070 --> 00:00:18.790
For the heck of it, I'll ask.

00:00:18.790 --> 00:00:21.540
Does this have anything
to do with school?

00:00:21.540 --> 00:00:22.600
Nope!

00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:23.900
That's right.

00:00:23.900 --> 00:00:25.710
As the leader of the student council,

00:00:25.710 --> 00:00:30.950
I need to ensure that its members
are thinking about their futures!

00:00:31.230 --> 00:00:32.850
You do, huh.

00:00:32.850 --> 00:00:36.370
Anyway, it helps to decide
what you want to be when

00:00:36.370 --> 00:00:38.210
you're still young.

00:00:38.210 --> 00:00:42.670
If you don't, you might
end up like Mafuyu-chan!

00:00:42.670 --> 00:00:44.260
What does that mean?

00:00:44.450 --> 00:00:46.170
That's a problem, yes.

00:00:46.750 --> 00:00:48.130
Guys?

00:00:48.590 --> 00:00:52.190
Once you're like Mafuyu-chan,
it's too late.

00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:58.780
Senpai, you just tore a gaping
hole in my heart, you know...

00:00:59.420 --> 00:01:00.410
That's right.

00:01:01.350 --> 00:01:03.740
I need to start thinking about this.

00:01:03.740 --> 00:01:07.650
Sis! You were totally looking
at me when you said that!

00:01:07.650 --> 00:01:09.250
We don't need two people

00:01:09.250 --> 00:01:11.580
in the student council with dead eyes.

00:01:11.980 --> 00:01:15.050
Who is the first person supposed to be?

00:01:15.050 --> 00:01:16.650
Tell me! Tell me!

00:01:16.650 --> 00:01:17.660
So!

00:01:18.020 --> 00:01:20.670
Let's think about what we want to be,

00:01:21.100 --> 00:01:23.750
and run a simulation.

00:02:54.930 --> 00:02:57.520
Mafuyu's just a loser.

00:02:57.520 --> 00:02:58.910
Nobody needs her.

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:03.120
Her value is going
down as we speak.

00:03:03.120 --> 00:03:06.170
Okay, who has something
they want to do?

00:03:06.170 --> 00:03:08.870
Me, me! Let me start!

00:03:09.180 --> 00:03:11.490
So you want to be a bride, right?

00:03:11.490 --> 00:03:12.880
Then I'll be your groom.

00:03:14.120 --> 00:03:15.660
No!

00:03:15.660 --> 00:03:17.130
That's not it.

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:20.020
What, you don't want to be a bride?

00:03:20.020 --> 00:03:22.790
N-No, I do, but...

00:03:23.330 --> 00:03:25.030
That's not it!

00:03:25.030 --> 00:03:27.800
I want to try a different job!

00:03:27.800 --> 00:03:30.090
A different job? Like what?

00:03:30.090 --> 00:03:32.400
I could be your partner, if you wanted.

00:03:32.960 --> 00:03:35.400
Really? Okay, then!

00:03:35.690 --> 00:03:37.170
Yeah, bring it on!

00:03:37.600 --> 00:03:39.900
I want to be a florist!

00:03:40.310 --> 00:03:42.530
In a cozy shop in front of the station.

00:03:42.960 --> 00:03:44.800
All the people in town love it,

00:03:45.210 --> 00:03:48.620
and it'll always be filled
with smiles and flowers!

00:03:49.330 --> 00:03:50.180
I can see it!

00:03:50.430 --> 00:03:52.760
I can see your flower shop!

00:03:52.760 --> 00:03:56.440
Welcome to Flower Shop Shiina!

00:03:57.920 --> 00:03:59.980
Flowers for your wife's birthday?

00:03:59.980 --> 00:04:00.930
That's wonderful.

00:04:01.160 --> 00:04:03.250
That personality doesn't suit you.

00:04:03.960 --> 00:04:05.960
F-Forget I said anything!

00:04:05.960 --> 00:04:11.480
Um, so... I'd like you to help me
find some flowers for my wife.

00:04:11.480 --> 00:04:14.010
Okay, leave it to me!

00:04:19.820 --> 00:04:23.340
By the way, what theme are
you basing your selections on?

00:04:23.340 --> 00:04:25.350
The theme I'm using is
"Combining Robots!"

00:04:25.700 --> 00:04:26.750
Why?

00:04:26.750 --> 00:04:28.950
Why am I getting Combining
Robot Flowers for my wife?

00:04:30.900 --> 00:04:33.470
The Ultimate Flower God Hanasakuda!

00:04:33.960 --> 00:04:36.260
It's 634 meters tall!

00:04:36.610 --> 00:04:38.460
You made that just now?

00:04:38.850 --> 00:04:42.120
Just make me a normal bouquet!

00:04:42.120 --> 00:04:43.290
Then take this.

00:04:44.140 --> 00:04:46.570
Four dandelions wrapped
in a rubber band.

00:04:46.570 --> 00:04:48.950
Am I supposed to be three years old?

00:04:48.950 --> 00:04:51.150
That'll be 39,800 yen.

00:04:51.150 --> 00:04:51.990
Expensive!

00:04:51.990 --> 00:04:54.750
If the dandelions cost that much,
then Hanasakuda must be...

00:04:54.750 --> 00:04:55.580
15 yen.

00:04:55.580 --> 00:04:56.600
Cheap!

00:04:56.600 --> 00:04:58.880
Then you're charging too much
for the dandelions!

00:04:59.250 --> 00:05:00.390
Shove it.

00:05:00.720 --> 00:05:03.080
Your normal personality shone
through for a second, there.

00:05:03.080 --> 00:05:05.060
You were totally getting
upset with a customer.

00:05:05.060 --> 00:05:06.940
Not at all!

00:05:06.940 --> 00:05:09.890
The three points of customer
service at Flower Shop Shiina are:

00:05:09.890 --> 00:05:12.600
Kindness, politeness, and blasphemy!

00:05:13.070 --> 00:05:14.110
What was that last one?

00:05:14.110 --> 00:05:14.970
What does that mean?

00:05:15.260 --> 00:05:17.260
I'll take those roses.

00:05:17.260 --> 00:05:18.060
Just give me those!

00:05:18.060 --> 00:05:19.010
Hand over the money, first.

00:05:20.020 --> 00:05:22.040
Where did that come from?

00:05:22.040 --> 00:05:22.700
Now!

00:05:22.700 --> 00:05:23.640
Right!

00:05:23.640 --> 00:05:24.680
Here you go.

00:05:25.280 --> 00:05:26.840
Cheapskate.

00:05:27.110 --> 00:05:28.180
Well, fine.

00:05:28.180 --> 00:05:28.850
Here you go.

00:05:29.980 --> 00:05:31.080
And now we're closed.

00:05:31.080 --> 00:05:34.380
I'd say we await your next visit,
but I'd be lying.

00:05:34.880 --> 00:05:36.950
Wait just a minute!

00:05:36.950 --> 00:05:38.660
I'd make a great florist!

00:05:38.660 --> 00:05:39.500
No way!

00:05:39.500 --> 00:05:41.560
Give me back my wallet.

00:05:43.220 --> 00:05:46.380
Mafuyu wants to try, too.

00:05:46.380 --> 00:05:49.330
Senpai, be my partner.

00:05:49.640 --> 00:05:50.910
Newlyweds?

00:05:50.910 --> 00:05:51.550
Yes!

00:05:51.550 --> 00:05:53.640
You didn't have to shoot
me down so quickly!

00:05:56.430 --> 00:05:59.720
Mafuyu wants to try being your wife.

00:06:01.600 --> 00:06:03.300
Welcome back, senpai.

00:06:03.900 --> 00:06:06.850
I mean, my darling.

00:06:10.460 --> 00:06:12.860
Okay, I'm ready for this!

00:06:13.170 --> 00:06:15.320
Mafuyu-chan, no, Mafuyu!

00:06:15.320 --> 00:06:16.380
I love you!

00:06:16.380 --> 00:06:18.330
Yes, Mafuyu loves you too!

00:06:19.510 --> 00:06:22.120
And that's the end of Student
Council's Discretion!

00:06:23.200 --> 00:06:24.480
Hey, now.

00:06:27.040 --> 00:06:28.690
Okay, okay then.

00:06:29.560 --> 00:06:31.640
Mafuyu, I'm back!

00:06:32.050 --> 00:06:33.950
Welcome home, darling.

00:06:33.950 --> 00:06:36.750
Will you start with dinner? Or a bath?

00:06:37.380 --> 00:06:38.520
Or...

00:06:39.390 --> 00:06:40.650
This is...

00:06:41.130 --> 00:06:42.750
...what I've been waiting for!

00:06:42.980 --> 00:06:44.890
Or Nakameguro-senpai?

00:06:46.400 --> 00:06:48.030
I didn't see that coming!

00:06:48.280 --> 00:06:49.460
No!

00:06:50.130 --> 00:06:51.210
Very well.

00:06:51.210 --> 00:06:52.760
Then I'll try again.

00:06:53.070 --> 00:06:56.090
Will you start with dinner? Or a bath?

00:06:56.090 --> 00:06:57.250
Or...

00:06:57.660 --> 00:06:58.790
Leveling up?

00:06:59.600 --> 00:07:02.040
I've just gotten home and
I have more work to do?

00:07:02.290 --> 00:07:05.810
We need to split the chores, darling.

00:07:05.810 --> 00:07:08.080
Leveling up counts as a chore?

00:07:08.080 --> 00:07:10.660
Oh, and about dinner...

00:07:10.660 --> 00:07:13.610
Good, you've at least got dinner ready—

00:07:13.610 --> 00:07:16.050
Mafuyu wants a sandwich tomorrow.

00:07:16.340 --> 00:07:19.290
I'm supposed to get it ready
before my wife wakes up?

00:07:20.700 --> 00:07:23.590
I've been busy making
doujinshi all day.

00:07:23.590 --> 00:07:24.810
I'm going to bed.

00:07:24.810 --> 00:07:26.100
Wait!

00:07:26.840 --> 00:07:28.000
What is it?

00:07:28.000 --> 00:07:29.860
Mafuyu's sleepy.

00:07:29.860 --> 00:07:30.930
A flower!

00:07:30.930 --> 00:07:32.210
I brought you a flower.

00:07:32.210 --> 00:07:33.710
A rose.

00:07:33.940 --> 00:07:37.580
The florist was crazy,
but I bought it for you.

00:07:38.890 --> 00:07:39.940
Mafuyu...

00:07:40.390 --> 00:07:42.580
Mafuyu is... disappointed in you!

00:07:43.650 --> 00:07:44.580
Why?

00:07:44.770 --> 00:07:47.270
Is a rose a bit too obvious?

00:07:47.270 --> 00:07:51.520
Why didn't you spend that
money on video games?

00:07:51.520 --> 00:07:52.220
What?

00:07:52.460 --> 00:07:55.070
Think about our family budget!

00:07:55.070 --> 00:07:58.810
I told you that 90% of
our living expenses must

00:07:58.810 --> 00:08:00.370
go to games, manga, and anime.

00:08:00.370 --> 00:08:01.230
Wait a second!

00:08:01.230 --> 00:08:03.050
That doesn't make sense.

00:08:03.050 --> 00:08:05.000
And look what you did!

00:08:05.000 --> 00:08:07.410
You're such an awful husband!

00:08:07.410 --> 00:08:08.910
I'm sorry, I guess.

00:08:08.910 --> 00:08:10.580
I thought you'd like it.

00:08:10.580 --> 00:08:11.830
Forget it.

00:08:11.830 --> 00:08:13.110
Mafuyu's going to bed.

00:08:13.110 --> 00:08:15.180
Make sure you level up, do the cooking,

00:08:15.180 --> 00:08:17.320
clean, do the laundry, and all that stuff.

00:08:18.190 --> 00:08:19.710
Goodnight!

00:08:20.960 --> 00:08:22.870
Goodnight.

00:08:23.520 --> 00:08:25.820
I was very happy!

00:08:25.820 --> 00:08:28.360
I may be getting betrothed soon!

00:08:28.860 --> 00:08:29.890
Yeah.

00:08:32.520 --> 00:08:33.760
Okay, Key-kun.

00:08:33.760 --> 00:08:36.230
Now you can be my partner.

00:08:37.050 --> 00:08:39.340
A simulation with you, Chizuru-san?

00:08:39.620 --> 00:08:41.070
It's okay.

00:08:41.070 --> 00:08:44.650
I'm sure you'll love it.

00:08:45.320 --> 00:08:46.610
What will you be?

00:08:47.190 --> 00:08:48.350
Your...

00:08:49.240 --> 00:08:50.430
...mistress.

00:08:54.990 --> 00:08:56.220
Mistress?

00:08:56.220 --> 00:08:57.510
Mistress...

00:08:57.510 --> 00:08:58.910
Mistress, huh?

00:08:59.870 --> 00:09:01.370
What's wrong, Key-kun?

00:09:01.370 --> 00:09:03.130
You talk about your harem all the time,

00:09:03.130 --> 00:09:05.160
you should be more excited.

00:09:05.160 --> 00:09:10.230
Sure, but I have Mafuyu-chan,
my future, beloved wife.

00:09:10.770 --> 00:09:11.840
Senpai...

00:09:12.580 --> 00:09:13.570
That's right.

00:09:13.570 --> 00:09:16.240
You have a wife who
spends all day playing

00:09:16.240 --> 00:09:18.400
video games, orders her husband around,

00:09:18.400 --> 00:09:21.410
wastes all the money,
and locks the bedroom door

00:09:21.410 --> 00:09:24.100
so you can't even touch her.

00:09:24.670 --> 00:09:25.870
Adultery is part of our culture!

00:09:26.280 --> 00:09:27.090
Senpai!

00:09:29.940 --> 00:09:31.720
Seriously.

00:09:32.240 --> 00:09:34.250
You wouldn't believe what
happened at the florist's,

00:09:34.250 --> 00:09:35.950
and then when I got home...

00:09:37.580 --> 00:09:39.000
There, there...

00:09:39.000 --> 00:09:40.330
Brush, brush.

00:09:40.830 --> 00:09:42.330
I love mistresses!

00:09:42.330 --> 00:09:44.740
They're just wonderful!

00:09:45.030 --> 00:09:48.890
If I can make your life better,
that's enough for me.

00:09:48.890 --> 00:09:51.240
Even if I can't be your wife.

00:09:51.400 --> 00:09:52.480
Chizuru.

00:09:52.910 --> 00:09:55.090
Oh no, I can't stop crying.

00:09:57.280 --> 00:10:01.400
I can feel someone who really
shouldn't be here staring at us,

00:10:01.400 --> 00:10:02.620
but let's ignore that!

00:10:02.620 --> 00:10:06.260
Okay! It's a mistress simulation,
so let's do something naughty!

00:10:06.600 --> 00:10:08.860
I made some food for you.

00:10:08.860 --> 00:10:11.220
You can enjoy it and then go home.

00:10:12.290 --> 00:10:14.850
I can't turn her down.

00:10:14.850 --> 00:10:17.200
Wh-What a horrible woman!

00:10:18.490 --> 00:10:21.660
I'm a professional mistress, after all.

00:10:21.660 --> 00:10:22.530
Professional?

00:10:22.530 --> 00:10:26.210
I graduated from the Tokyo School
of Mistress Skills.

00:10:26.210 --> 00:10:28.000
Mistress Skills?

00:10:28.000 --> 00:10:31.540
For some reason, I'm not
feeling the love anymore.

00:10:31.540 --> 00:10:32.650
Come on, Key-kun.

00:10:33.350 --> 00:10:36.950
Stop complaining and try
my home cooked meal.

00:10:37.270 --> 00:10:40.320
What kind of food do you
use to win a man's heart?

00:10:40.320 --> 00:10:42.280
Beef stew's a pretty obvious choice.

00:10:42.280 --> 00:10:43.230
Soy sauce.

00:10:43.630 --> 00:10:44.630
Soy sauce?

00:10:44.630 --> 00:10:47.090
I made it with lots of love.

00:10:47.090 --> 00:10:48.850
Soy sauce? From scratch?

00:10:48.850 --> 00:10:50.460
Starting with soy beans.

00:10:50.460 --> 00:10:52.340
That's amazing, but...

00:10:52.850 --> 00:10:55.970
You're telling me you can't even drink
a single bottle of my soy sauce?

00:10:55.970 --> 00:11:00.070
I can't drink a whole bottle of
soy sauce, no matter whose it is.

00:11:00.070 --> 00:11:01.000
I see.

00:11:01.000 --> 00:11:02.280
I'm sorry.

00:11:02.280 --> 00:11:04.750
I've overstepped my boundaries
as your mistress.

00:11:04.750 --> 00:11:07.250
Glare...

00:11:08.460 --> 00:11:10.760
They're staring at me like
I'm an enemy of womankind.

00:11:12.720 --> 00:11:14.640
Why don't you head home?

00:11:14.640 --> 00:11:15.830
You got bored, didn't you!

00:11:15.830 --> 00:11:18.760
You totally got bored with
playing mistress, right now!

00:11:18.760 --> 00:11:20.520
Fine.

00:11:20.520 --> 00:11:22.530
I'll leave, then.

00:11:24.440 --> 00:11:25.160
Um...

00:11:25.490 --> 00:11:26.540
Well.

00:11:27.310 --> 00:11:28.470
Come back.

00:11:29.080 --> 00:11:31.480
I'll come every day!

00:11:31.780 --> 00:11:33.450
Mistresses Banzai!

00:11:33.980 --> 00:11:34.160
Tokyo Institute for Mistress Skills

00:11:34.160 --> 00:11:36.790
That lifestyle sounds pretty good.

00:11:36.790 --> 00:11:38.720
I wonder how many men I could
have going at one time.

00:11:38.940 --> 00:11:40.120
Is she evil?

00:11:40.120 --> 00:11:42.660
That school really exists, then?

00:11:42.660 --> 00:11:43.990
Ahem.

00:11:43.990 --> 00:11:46.320
I am the company president!

00:11:47.450 --> 00:11:51.460
The only job I could have
is company president!

00:11:51.810 --> 00:11:52.650
President!

00:11:58.780 --> 00:12:00.570
The only job I could have
is company president!

00:12:00.820 --> 00:12:02.730
President!

00:12:02.730 --> 00:12:06.960
President, we've got lots
of cute girls at our club.

00:12:07.630 --> 00:12:09.710
Then I'll come here today.

00:12:09.710 --> 00:12:11.190
Who are you?

00:12:11.190 --> 00:12:14.620
I want to be a real company president!

00:12:17.560 --> 00:12:19.690
I am the company president!

00:12:19.690 --> 00:12:22.020
Good morning, President.

00:12:22.020 --> 00:12:23.410
Yes, good morning.

00:12:23.410 --> 00:12:26.020
Get to work.

00:12:26.020 --> 00:12:26.660
Right.

00:12:27.060 --> 00:12:28.090
It's no good.

00:12:28.090 --> 00:12:31.170
I can't picture this at all.

00:12:31.170 --> 00:12:34.640
By the way, President,
what does our company do?

00:12:35.050 --> 00:12:36.950
We're a temp staffing agency!

00:12:36.950 --> 00:12:38.280
What else would we be?

00:12:38.280 --> 00:12:40.190
What else, indeed...

00:12:40.190 --> 00:12:42.110
So, what exactly do we do?

00:12:42.110 --> 00:12:45.550
You go to a bunch of
different companies,

00:12:45.550 --> 00:12:49.090
make money, and give it to me.

00:12:49.960 --> 00:12:53.490
Doesn't that just mean
I'm giving you money?

00:12:53.940 --> 00:12:56.010
And we make two trillion yen a year.

00:12:56.940 --> 00:12:58.720
I'm working really hard, aren't I?

00:12:59.170 --> 00:13:02.180
But your net salary is 90,000.

00:13:02.180 --> 00:13:04.180
That's the monthly pay for part time!

00:13:05.360 --> 00:13:06.600
That's yearly.

00:13:06.600 --> 00:13:09.270
That's worse than part time...

00:13:09.730 --> 00:13:13.640
By the way, my salary is
two trillion minus 90,000 yen.

00:13:13.640 --> 00:13:15.440
You're taking too much.

00:13:15.440 --> 00:13:19.090
And where are we getting
our operating funds?

00:13:19.090 --> 00:13:21.040
You handle that.

00:13:21.040 --> 00:13:22.520
I'm working too hard!

00:13:22.650 --> 00:13:24.100
Enough.

00:13:24.100 --> 00:13:25.890
Get to your first job.

00:13:26.950 --> 00:13:28.400
Bye, then.

00:13:28.400 --> 00:13:29.570
Wait, Sugisaki.

00:13:29.570 --> 00:13:30.660
Where are you going?

00:13:30.990 --> 00:13:32.900
Where? My job.

00:13:32.900 --> 00:13:37.370
Then use that transporter
instead of the door.

00:13:37.370 --> 00:13:38.860
A transporter?

00:13:39.360 --> 00:13:42.370
How far in the future is this
simulation taking place?

00:13:42.370 --> 00:13:45.050
It's when I graduate from
university, so maybe,

00:13:45.050 --> 00:13:46.540
five years from now?

00:13:46.830 --> 00:13:49.510
Japan's technology advances fast.

00:13:49.870 --> 00:13:51.880
Get going, Sugisaki.

00:13:51.880 --> 00:13:56.150
I'll watch over the blue Earth
you're visiting from here.

00:13:57.340 --> 00:13:58.160
The Earth?

00:14:00.310 --> 00:14:02.160
Where is our company?

00:14:02.530 --> 00:14:04.400
Stop talking and go!

00:14:04.850 --> 00:14:08.670
At this rate, they'll cause the
Earth to smash into the sun!

00:14:08.910 --> 00:14:10.510
What's going on right now?

00:14:10.510 --> 00:14:11.430
Who are "they"?

00:14:11.430 --> 00:14:13.170
Is this the time to be working?

00:14:13.430 --> 00:14:15.340
You can do it, Sugisaki!

00:14:15.340 --> 00:14:17.550
All the experience you've
gained from the jobs you've

00:14:17.550 --> 00:14:20.580
had until this point have prepared
you for this final battle!

00:14:20.580 --> 00:14:22.330
For some reason that sounds awesome!

00:14:22.330 --> 00:14:24.500
I'm all fired up!

00:14:24.890 --> 00:14:27.950
Sugisaki Ken, off to go do his best!

00:14:30.040 --> 00:14:32.860
Someday, your efforts will save the Earth—
No, the universe—

00:14:32.860 --> 00:14:35.880
No, all of spacetime itself!

00:14:35.880 --> 00:14:38.600
Go, super temp employee, Sugisaki!

00:14:38.830 --> 00:14:39.790
Aye aye, sir!

00:14:41.100 --> 00:14:41.970
Not happening!

00:14:42.980 --> 00:14:44.320
Don't get mad.

00:14:44.320 --> 00:14:45.940
Come on, it was fun.

00:14:45.940 --> 00:14:48.340
We're doing a job simulation right now!

00:14:48.340 --> 00:14:50.900
Not enjoying some science fiction!

00:14:50.900 --> 00:14:52.110
Minatsu is right.

00:14:52.350 --> 00:14:56.080
You need to stop screwing around
and do a real simulation.

00:14:57.290 --> 00:15:01.390
We were in the realm of fiction the instant
she declared herself company president.

00:15:02.140 --> 00:15:03.340
F-Forget it!

00:15:03.340 --> 00:15:04.790
I don't wanna be the president of a company!

00:15:06.610 --> 00:15:11.010
There are other things I want to be.

00:15:12.820 --> 00:15:14.740
The criminal is in this room.

00:15:15.440 --> 00:15:19.110
I'll explain the hidden
trick behind this case.

00:15:19.110 --> 00:15:20.270
Wait a second!

00:15:20.270 --> 00:15:21.210
What's your problem?

00:15:21.210 --> 00:15:23.180
This is the climax.

00:15:23.180 --> 00:15:25.740
The climax of what, exactly?

00:15:26.110 --> 00:15:27.360
A detective.

00:15:28.220 --> 00:15:30.090
That's what Aka-chan wants to be.

00:15:30.470 --> 00:15:31.480
Right?

00:15:31.480 --> 00:15:32.170
Yes.

00:15:32.170 --> 00:15:34.350
I want to be a famous detective.

00:15:34.700 --> 00:15:36.110
By the way, president...

00:15:36.110 --> 00:15:38.380
You can call me detective.

00:15:38.860 --> 00:15:40.030
President.

00:15:42.360 --> 00:15:43.790
Detective?

00:15:43.790 --> 00:15:45.360
What is it, young Sugisaki?

00:15:45.530 --> 00:15:46.830
Annoying.

00:15:47.240 --> 00:15:49.600
You talked about solving the case,

00:15:49.600 --> 00:15:51.370
but when was there a case?

00:15:51.890 --> 00:15:54.360
Don't tell me you've
already forgotten!

00:15:54.360 --> 00:15:55.640
Young Sugisaki.

00:15:56.010 --> 00:16:02.810
That first shocking crime
that started everything.

00:16:03.700 --> 00:16:06.150
I'm gonna have to go along
with this again, aren't I?

00:16:06.590 --> 00:16:08.090
Mystery on the high-speed express:

00:16:08.090 --> 00:16:09.850
The case of the missing, frozen orange.

00:16:10.540 --> 00:16:16.070
As the name indicates, it was
a sad and complicated case.

00:16:16.460 --> 00:16:20.570
It seems kind of silly to me.

00:16:22.540 --> 00:16:25.070
Just remembering it
now makes me shudder.

00:16:25.620 --> 00:16:29.570
The frozen orange I was
planning to eat...

00:16:29.880 --> 00:16:33.120
It disappeared while I was
inspecting the train!

00:16:33.570 --> 00:16:35.390
So you're the victim?

00:16:35.390 --> 00:16:39.460
After much effort, I solved the
trick behind that impossible crime.

00:16:39.460 --> 00:16:41.220
You're exaggerating too much.

00:16:41.530 --> 00:16:43.490
The trick was... It was...

00:16:44.260 --> 00:16:48.730
That the frozen orange melted
and became a regular orange!

00:16:48.970 --> 00:16:50.800
Wh-What?

00:16:51.910 --> 00:16:53.870
That's not a crime at all!

00:16:54.460 --> 00:16:56.330
And the second crime...

00:16:56.330 --> 00:16:59.360
It happened at the snowy inn:
the early bedtime incident.

00:17:00.830 --> 00:17:02.610
It was terrible.

00:17:03.230 --> 00:17:05.820
And strange.

00:17:06.830 --> 00:17:11.610
It was our class field trip,
and I'd been looking forward to it,

00:17:11.610 --> 00:17:14.090
but I fell asleep at 8:00
instead of 9:00, like I usually do.

00:17:14.090 --> 00:17:15.620
That doesn't matter!

00:17:15.930 --> 00:17:19.890
The biggest mystery was that
my watch was off by an hour.

00:17:20.080 --> 00:17:22.070
Your fault again!

00:17:22.070 --> 00:17:25.130
You're just telling
me about some mistakes

00:17:25.130 --> 00:17:26.990
you made on the field trip, aren't you?

00:17:27.380 --> 00:17:30.130
And on the fourth day, it happened.

00:17:30.770 --> 00:17:33.140
The case of the missing
Sakurano Kurimu.

00:17:33.330 --> 00:17:36.910
Oh, come to think of it, you got lost.

00:17:39.290 --> 00:17:40.710
Hey, Chizuru!

00:17:40.710 --> 00:17:43.410
I was about to do my
big deduction scene!

00:17:43.700 --> 00:17:45.940
No, the case is solved.

00:17:45.940 --> 00:17:48.050
Sakurano Kurimu got lost...

00:17:48.050 --> 00:17:49.920
I didn't get lost! I went missing!

00:17:50.150 --> 00:17:53.360
But it's only a crime
if there's a criminal.

00:17:53.360 --> 00:17:56.930
And all of that was your own fault.

00:17:57.450 --> 00:17:58.770
That's not true.

00:17:58.770 --> 00:18:00.070
I can tell!

00:18:00.070 --> 00:18:02.080
There was a criminal behind
all of those evil acts!

00:18:02.080 --> 00:18:07.560
Um, I don't think a third party
could've done any of those.

00:18:07.560 --> 00:18:08.570
They could!

00:18:08.570 --> 00:18:11.330
I just realized a while
ago that there was one

00:18:11.330 --> 00:18:13.080
person who could've done it!

00:18:13.340 --> 00:18:15.080
Who?

00:18:15.460 --> 00:18:17.080
I told you.

00:18:17.080 --> 00:18:19.320
The criminal is in this room.

00:18:20.560 --> 00:18:23.270
Wh-Why aren't you guys more surprised?

00:18:23.270 --> 00:18:26.090
Don't look at me like I'm stupid!

00:18:26.090 --> 00:18:29.590
There<i> is</i> a real criminal!

00:18:30.360 --> 00:18:33.790
The detective started crying
before explaining her deductions.

00:18:34.800 --> 00:18:37.550
Are you satisfied now, Aka-chan?

00:18:38.520 --> 00:18:41.140
There is a criminal!

00:18:41.330 --> 00:18:43.980
Yeah, there is.

00:18:44.210 --> 00:18:47.110
Now be a good girl and sleep.

00:18:47.840 --> 00:18:49.300
I'm not going to sleep.

00:18:49.300 --> 00:18:51.850
I'm not... tired...

00:18:53.100 --> 00:18:54.100
She fell asleep!

00:18:54.100 --> 00:18:55.980
That saved us.

00:18:55.980 --> 00:18:58.190
Thanks, Akaba-senpai.

00:18:58.190 --> 00:18:59.860
There's no need to thank me.

00:19:00.440 --> 00:19:04.630
As the criminal, it's my job
to silence the detective.

00:19:08.780 --> 00:19:13.430
I was behind all of the cases.

00:19:14.470 --> 00:19:18.880
Aka-chan was going to eat an
orange that was frozen solid,

00:19:18.880 --> 00:19:21.590
and I thought she might hurt
her nails or something.

00:19:22.060 --> 00:19:25.150
So I told her to look at the
rest of the cars on the train.

00:19:25.460 --> 00:19:28.190
But I didn't think she'd spend

00:19:28.190 --> 00:19:31.120
so much time exploring
that it'd totally melt.

00:19:31.120 --> 00:19:34.260
So that was her fault, then.

00:19:35.090 --> 00:19:37.410
Next was her going to bed early.

00:19:38.330 --> 00:19:42.770
She wasn't able to sleep on
the train, so she was tired.

00:19:43.030 --> 00:19:46.540
So I adjusted her watch
so she'd go to bed early.

00:19:46.990 --> 00:19:52.900
I didn't want her to be too
tired to enjoy the field trip.

00:19:52.900 --> 00:19:57.330
Has there even been such
a compassionate criminal?

00:19:57.810 --> 00:19:59.940
And compared to that, the president...

00:19:59.940 --> 00:20:04.060
Everyone, if you want your dreams to

00:20:04.060 --> 00:20:06.720
come true, you have to work hard.

00:20:06.720 --> 00:20:11.100
Even if I graduate and can't
look after you anymore,

00:20:11.100 --> 00:20:14.430
you still have to find a way to get by.

00:20:15.000 --> 00:20:15.920
President...

00:20:22.920 --> 00:20:26.590
If I fall asleep during the day,
I can't sleep at night.

00:20:27.920 --> 00:20:31.810
Come to think of it, I didn't
hear what Sugisaki wants to do.

00:20:31.810 --> 00:20:33.560
What I want to do?

00:20:34.840 --> 00:20:36.760
My dream...

00:20:38.080 --> 00:20:39.390
I just want...

00:20:39.830 --> 00:20:41.740
...to be with everyone.

00:20:42.990 --> 00:20:44.400
You want what?

00:20:45.470 --> 00:20:48.280
Maybe I'll start a company.

00:20:48.870 --> 00:20:50.640
You want to be a CEO?

00:20:50.970 --> 00:20:51.580
Yes.

00:20:51.980 --> 00:20:54.770
And I'll hire everyone here.

00:20:57.690 --> 00:21:01.790
You couldn't pull off being a CEO.

00:21:01.790 --> 00:21:05.520
Well, if you paid me,
I could work with you.

00:21:05.870 --> 00:21:09.150
I think you'd do better as
an unsuccessful author.

00:21:09.520 --> 00:21:12.420
Stay indoors, like Mafuyu does!

00:21:12.940 --> 00:21:15.660
People who want to
run a company just for

00:21:15.660 --> 00:21:17.800
the sake of it never succeed.

00:21:18.200 --> 00:21:20.200
Thought you might if I helped you.

00:21:21.070 --> 00:21:22.760
That's not fair!

00:21:22.760 --> 00:21:25.440
Then I'll be the president
of that company.

00:21:26.560 --> 00:21:29.170
You said earlier that you
didn't want to be a president.

00:21:30.820 --> 00:21:32.940
Then I'll run your board of directors!

00:21:32.940 --> 00:21:36.400
That's right, I'm always
going to be on top.

00:21:36.400 --> 00:21:38.670
That's me! Always on top!

00:21:38.670 --> 00:21:40.220
You're nuts.

00:21:40.220 --> 00:21:42.420
But that sounds like you.

00:21:43.450 --> 00:21:45.020
Everyone's following their own path.

00:21:45.950 --> 00:21:47.460
Those two are graduating.

00:21:47.890 --> 00:21:49.460
And those two are transferring schools.

00:21:50.110 --> 00:21:54.100
Either way, we won't be the
student council for much longer...

00:21:54.100 --> 00:21:55.920
Or high schoolers.

00:21:55.920 --> 00:21:58.890
Or kids, or students.

00:21:59.860 --> 00:22:03.210
Sugisaki, what are you doing?

00:22:03.210 --> 00:22:04.980
Hurry up or I'll
leave you behind!

00:22:07.080 --> 00:22:08.310
That's right.

00:22:09.100 --> 00:22:10.550
Did you say something?

00:22:10.860 --> 00:22:12.680
Nope.

00:22:13.940 --> 00:22:14.840
That's right.

00:22:15.510 --> 00:22:19.810
I realized it wasn't important that we be

00:22:19.810 --> 00:22:21.320
student council members forever.

00:23:57.460 --> 00:24:00.290
Um, about the president getting lost...

00:24:00.550 --> 00:24:01.360
Yes.

00:24:01.360 --> 00:24:02.850
I was behind that, too.

00:24:02.850 --> 00:24:05.800
I deliberately separated
her from everyone else.

00:24:05.800 --> 00:24:06.920
Separated her?

00:24:06.920 --> 00:24:10.000
Th-There was a good reason
for that, too, right?

00:24:10.000 --> 00:24:11.300
Yes, of course.

00:24:11.650 --> 00:24:14.170
I wanted to videotape her wandering
around and calling my name.

00:24:14.170 --> 00:24:15.870
<i>Chizuru! Where are you? Chizuru?</i>

00:24:15.870 --> 00:24:17.830
She was so cute.

00:24:17.830 --> 00:24:18.310
<i>Chizuru! Where are you? Chizuru?</i>

00:24:19.860 --> 00:24:24.510
That part was really evil!

00:24:25.980 --> 00:24:27.360
Project Genocide.

00:24:27.360 --> 00:24:29.880
We'll turn Hekiyou Academy students into otaku.

00:24:29.890 --> 00:24:31.190
We'll make toilet air fresheners

00:24:31.190 --> 00:24:32.300
smell like yakisoba bread.

00:24:32.300 --> 00:24:33.530
I'm not pregnant!

00:24:33.530 --> 00:24:35.300
What's going to happen?

00:24:35.300 --> 00:24:37.110
The Student Council Reclaims

00:24:37.110 --> 00:24:39.200
See the truth for yourself!
